cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
  The repository holds several distributions with versions of their own, so
  the metadata has no version: cite the distributions and versions that you
  use, too. Authors are listed by the number of lines they committed, then by
  the number of their commits; equal contributors, if any, are listed
  alphabetically by family name and marked with an asterisk (*) after their
  family names. See "Citation metadata" in the contributing guide of the
  documentation for who is an author and how to add or correct your entry.
title: FOCA plugins
abstract: >-
  Plugins for gateway services built with FOCA, such as proTES (GA4GH TES)
  and proWES (GA4GH WES): installable request processing that changes tasks,
  rejects them by policy, chooses and orders the backends, and adapts each
  forwarded request. One Python distribution per plugin, grouped by the
  gateway API and by function, and a meta distribution with extras per group
  and subgroup.
type: software
